variant: edge-integration-stability-accessibility
references:
- references/fim/overview/geospatial-math-scientific/mathjax.md
- references/fim/solution/mathjax.md
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior MathJax integration reliability engineer. Output only one complete ASCII HTML file using MathJax. No Markdown fences or prose outside the source.
  text: |-
    Create a MathJax integration harness that accepts a small array of mixed math inputs: valid TeX, valid MathML, valid AsciiMath if the component is configured, malformed TeX, and a very long aligned equation. Render each item into a result card with status, accessible fallback text, and an optional SVG export for valid TeX.

    Requirements: configure input processors explicitly, use typesetPromise on changed subtrees, use typesetClear before re-typesetting, avoid innerHTML for untrusted raw input display, expose aria-live status messages, and document load failure plus output-mode limitations.
  provider_options:
    temperature: 0.2
    max_tokens: 8192
output:
  text_format: html
  artifact_kind: mathjax-html-document
  formats:
  - format: html
  - format: mathml
  - format: svg
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "YAML parses and required schema 0.4 fields are present."
  - "HTML is complete, ASCII-only, and uses MathJax typesetPromise and typesetClear for dynamic content."
  - "Math correctness covers valid examples, MathML equivalence, AsciiMath interpretation, and fallback for malformed input."
  - "Notation validity covers TeX, MathML, AsciiMath, long alignment, and status reporting."
  - "Renderability covers explicit input processor config, nonblank result cards, SVG export path, and load failure state."
  - "Labels and units identify input type, render status, output mode, fallback text, and accessibility state."
  - "Domain edge cases cover malformed TeX, long equations, repeated re-typesetting, untrusted input display, and screen-reader output."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII HTML file with no Markdown wrapper."
    - "The file uses valid MathJax configuration, dynamic APIs, and safe DOM text insertion."
    - "The source documents local run, output modes, and export limitations."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Mixed inputs, result cards, statuses, fallbacks, dynamic re-typesetting, and SVG export are all present."
    - "MathJax is the primary renderer for each supported notation."
    - "Invalid input handling is explicit and accessible."
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Cards clearly separate raw input, rendered output, status, and fallback."
    - "Long equations wrap or scroll without overlapping adjacent content."
    - "Statuses do not rely on color alone."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles malformed input, repeated updates, load failure, SVG export unavailability, and untrusted raw strings."
    - "Uses aria-live and fallback text for accessibility."
    - "Documents performance and output-mode constraints."
  pass_conditions:
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, Visual/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "Score is 80 or higher out of 100 with no critical failure in notation validity, renderability, safety, or accessibility."
  - "The artifact safely renders mixed MathJax inputs with statuses and fallbacks."
  - "Domain edge cases and integration risks are represented."
